what a day you've had you were across  the country earlier today are you okay  yeah like what time is it I don't even  know what day it is  don't even tell me a date I have no idea  we're like for four days past the World  Cup that's all I know I mean you were in  Europe like what time zone are you in  you know yeah I mean I have no idea I  think it's like 6:00 a.m. in France  right now so running on fumes but I mean  it's not hard when you have this in your  hand and I mean look you go from New  York and all that cheering and all that  celebrating and then you got to get glam  yeah I was this night emotional for you  was it exciting what was going through  your mind out on that stage just  excitement and also just feeling proud  to have like my family and attendance as  well they like I always say like they're  on vacation when I'm playing but they're  really not like they're on this roller  coaster with us and like every four days  we play a game and like it's so  exhausting and it takes everything out  of me and then we need to pick it back  up and do it four days later in a World  Cup seven times in a row and like my  families along along the right too so I  think tonight we're just like enjoying  enjoy I mean you guys have been fighting  to go out and freaking win the World Cup  for us but also fight for women and  fight for equal pay and you had a lot of  cheerleaders tonight Billie Jean was  here you know so many people how does  that feel for you to feel that support  from other female athletes  it's incredible these are the women that  really paved the way and so for us to  kind of fall in the footsteps and kind  of now bare some of that responsibility  and take that with pride it means a lot  so yeah she was she was the first and  miss a word for you I mean I you got to  take this moment in a little bit are you  in shock are you feeling I'm feeling  good yeah I guess I'm still a little  like taking it in a little bit but  obviously it's an incredible award and  there's been so many amazing women that  I have watched go on the stage and get  this award as I've been to many ESPYs  before so it's great to know be that  woman and I mean you guys have had a lot  to say over the past couple months  you've had a lot to say in the face of  some criticism what did you want to say  with your speech tonight so I wanted to  say that we need to invest in women and  when you've invested in women you see  the return on it the World Cup was a  perfect example of it of the fact that  yes I know we give you a soccer and  extremely hard time  but you have to give them credit for  investing in this team over the course  of the last 20 years and you could see  that in the World Cup how dominant we  were and teams that weren't so dominant  but have the potential don't have the  investment from their country from their  Federation from from the people who  might now respect to the sport as much  so I think investing in women's sports  is so crucial how do you feel about how  everything went in New York today you  guys had so many people cheering for you  rightfully so but you know there there  is still things hanging over your head  of the cause that you're fighting for  yeah I think that today we were just  enjoying actually the last couple days  we were enjoying it it's not without  some tough questions of course which  we're willing to face head-on but this  morning we were just overwhelmed with  the support and you know and when you're  in France for a month  playing for a World Cup you don't  realize the impacts that we have on this  country over a short period of time and  the amount of eyes that are watching so  we got a glimpse of that this morning  and it was quite incredible we were  talking earlier about everything megan's  had to say too about how awesome it was  to hear say this team has new black  girls white girls straight girls gay  girls and how amazing that it was like  is she like a rapper no she's like  rhyming and all this and like the best  public speaker ever I'm like okay you  have like a job anywhere you want after  that speech like for her to be able to  say that you know that's women's  different sexualities or not something  they could always talk about you know  and how have you guys you know kind of  soak that in as a team that like you've  paved the way in so many ways yeah I  think we're all about inclusivity and I  think that we say that every single day  I think we walk the walk and Meghan's a  prime example of someone who is willing  to stand up for what she believes in and  and speak her mind on it and I think  that that's kind of giving us a little  motivation and courage to do to do the  same on the team so it's pretty great to  have her as a teammate  she's been incredible and she's I'm so  happy to have her on my side and I saw a  tweet that I can't stop thinking about a  guy from the ringer tweeted the women's  soccer team said we're gonna turn down  an invite from the White House then they  went and won the World Cup that's the  biggest flex ever I mean if you guys  talked about that anymore how are you  feeling as you as you move forward after  New York  we've talked a little bit about it but  it's kind of been a whirlwind of a  couple of days we really need to sit  down and talk more about it and have a  real discussion about it because of  course the White House is more than just  one person but at the same time the one  person you know that is the most  important person doesn't doesn't agree  on a lot of things that we are and who  and what we really talk about and and  who we are so I think that's really  difficult so I think we'll have to talk  about it for now we're just enjoying and  celebrating and obviously in the next  couple of weeks there'll be some tough  decisions to make have you heard from  him at all no we haven't got a formal  invitation just a tweet tweet I got to  tell you all night long we've been  having people do the tea sip I never  okay I like this can you give it to us  one more time we got to get it from the  expert I mean it's better with champagne  but I'll do it with the trophy fine  [Music]

